<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n6932" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀναλογ-ιστικός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>judging by analogy, analogical,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				S.E.
				<u>M.</u>
				11.250
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ -κὴ τέχνη</span> ib. <i><span class="en">
				1.214
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> of knowledge,
			etc., <i>reflective,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Phld.
				<u>Herc.</u>
				1003
			</span></i>. Adv.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-κῶς</span> ibid. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>teaching analogy,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γραμματικοί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.E.
					<u>M.</u>
					2.59
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἵρεσις -κή,</span> of the
			Rational or Dogmatic school of physicians, opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπιλογιστική</span> (the Empirics), <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				1.65
			</span></i>; <i>analogisticus sermo</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Subf.Emp.</u>
				8p.52Bonnet.
			</span></i>
			Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-κῶς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.E.
					<u>M.</u>
					3.40
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				18(2).346
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
